cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Replication package on LLM adherence on Project Euler problems
message: >-
  If you use this replication package, the generated corpora, or the adherence
  analyser, please cite the preprint under "preferred-citation" below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chandimal
    family-names: Adikari
  - given-names: Nandika
    family-names: Herath
repository-code: https://github.com/researchartifacts/ProjectEulerAIEvaluation
abstract: >-
  Generated code corpora, static adherence analyser, and execution harness for an
  empirical study of cost-efficient large language models on Project Euler
  problems under two prompting conditions. Licensing is mixed: the authors' own
  code is MIT, the generated corpora carry no ownership claim, and no Project
  Euler content is redistributed. See LICENSE, NOTICE and CORPUS_TERMS.md.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - code generation
  - empirical software engineering
  - replication package
  - Project Euler
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    An Empirical Evaluation of Cost-Efficient Large Language Models on
    Algorithmic Programming Tasks
  authors:
    - given-names: Chandimal
      family-names: Adikari
    - given-names: Nandika
      family-names: Herath
  year: 2026
  url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.18052
  identifiers:
    - type: other
      value: arXiv:2609.18052
      description: arXiv preprint identifier
